  "title": "A much wider model shelf",
  "summary": "The model catalog expanded across text, images, video, speech, and music while the routes and tools around it got easier to trust and use.\n\nGrok 4.7, GLM-5.3 FlashX, Claude Opus 5.5, GPT-6 Sol and Luna, GPT-5.3 Codex, and MiMo V2.6 Flash and Pro joined the text catalog. Several support roughly million-token contexts. Ling 3.0 Flash VL added video input, and GPT-6 Sol and Luna gained access for Quest Pollen accounts without requiring a paid balance. More choices are useful when you can actually find the one that fits.\n\nMAI Image 2.6 and 2.6 Flash, FLUX 1.1 Pro, Qwen Image 2.1, and Recraft V4.1 Flash expanded image generation and editing. MiniMax H3 Max added video generation with synchronized audio; Gemini 3.8 Flash and Flash Lite added speech with 30 voices; and Lyria 3.5 added text-to-MP3 songs. Floret can also turn a prompt, optionally paired with an image, into a downloadable 3D asset.\n\nMistral Small 4 gained a direct route, direct Vertex routes returned as the primary path for Gemini models, and seven model routes were replaced ahead of Fireworks’ serverless shutdown. MiniMax M2.7 now reaches M2.7 rather than M3, while Sonar moved to Perplexity’s Agent API with citations and its existing Pollinations endpoints intact. Three community routers offer different ways to choose models by task, capabilities, price, and recent health. Model-list filtering now uses recent reliability for public community proxies, with an option to include otherwise accessible models excluded by that filter.\n\nEnter’s Models, Agents, and MCP tabs returned with clearer navigation. Model cards now show access, pricing options, usage rates, and supported variants more distinctly; the catalog also shows the sample behind reliability labels. Key setup gained model search and filtering, while sign-in, authorization, and account screens got clearer guidance. The price display changed, not the rates.",
  "pr_count": 86,
